<p>I mentioned in <a href="https://leancrew.com/all-this/2026/11/steve-monty-and-julia/">my last post</a> that I’m learning <a href="https://julialang.org/">Julia</a>. I intend to use it for mathematical work, and because Greek letters are used in formulas I’ll be turning into programs, it seemed like a good idea to make it easier to include Greek letters in my code as variable names. Over the weekend, I made a simple Typinator set for that purpose.<sup id="fnref:editor"><a href="#fn:editor" rel="footnote">1</a></sup></p>
<p>You can <a href="https://leancrew.com/all-this/downloads/Greek%20letters.tyset.zip">download the Typinator set</a> if you think it would be helpful to you. Here’s a list of the Greek letters and their abbreviations.</p>
