<p>I tend to use the prime and double prime symbols for feet and inches, hence the <code>ft</code> and <code>in</code> in their abbreviations. In the past, I’ve used different abbreviations for some of these, like <code>;times</code> and <code>;divide</code> for × and ÷.</p>
<p>A note on the downloads: The two Typinator sets are saved on the server as zip files. Depending on how your browser is configured, they may or may not expand immediately when downloaded. Once they’re expanded, you can add them to your Typinator setup by double-clicking or dragging them into the Typinator window.</p>
<p>Simple little automations like this often save me more time than the more complex ones I often write about. We’ll see how these work out.</p>
